{"ref":"2018.MM43.10","summary":"Crossing Lake Shore Boulevard West at Colborne Lodge Drive is a problem for pedestrians and cyclists, due to the need for increased road markings, and the lack of a safe space on the east side median for those to stop. Tragically the recent death of a cyclist when a vehicle went through a red light at the intersection has highlighted the need for action to be taken.","decided":"City Council on June 26, 27, 28 and 29, 2018, adopted the following: 1. City Council direct the General Manager, Transportation Services, under the lens of Vision Zero, to review the interactions of pedestrians, cyclists and vehicles at the intersection of Lake Shore Boulevard West and Colborne Lodge Drive, and to implement any changes necessary to promote the safety of all users.","motions":[{"stage":"City Council","when":"","desc":"Two-Thirds required - MM43.10 - Waive referral","type":"Waive Referral","result":"Carried, 36-5","yes":36,"no":5,"votes":[["Ana Bailão","Yes"],["Cesar Palacio","Yes"],["Christin Carmichael Greb","Yes"],["David Shiner","Yes"],["Frances Nunziata","Yes"],["Frank Di Giorgio","Yes"],["Gary Crawford","Yes"],["Glenn De Baeremaeker","Yes"],["Gord Perks","Yes"],["James Pasternak","Yes"],["Janet Davis","Yes"],["Jaye Robinson","Yes"],["Jim Hart","Yes"],["Jim Karygiannis","Yes"],["Joe Cressy","Yes"],["Joe Mihevc","Yes"],["John Filion","Yes"],["Josh Colle","Yes"],["Josh Matlow","Yes"],["Justin J. Di Ciano","Yes"],["Kristyn Wong-Tam","Yes"],["Lucy Troisi","Yes"],["Maria Augimeri","Yes"],["Mark Grimes","Yes"],["Mary Fragedakis","Yes"],["Mary-Margaret McMahon","Yes"],["Michael Thompson","Yes"],["Michelle Holland","Yes"],["Miganoush Megardichian","Yes"],["Mike Layton","Yes"],["Neethan Shan","Yes"],["Norman Kelly","Yes"],["Paul Ainslie","Yes"],["Paula Fletcher","Yes"],["Sarah Doucette","Yes"],["Vincent Crisanti","Yes"],["Denzil Minnan-Wong","No"],["Giorgio Mammoliti","No"],["John Campbell","No"],["Michael Ford","No"],["Stephen Holyday","No"],["Anth